    "en": {
      "caveats": "The abstract does not provide specific empirical data, sample sizes, or a concrete case study evaluation for the framework.",
      "what": "This paper presents a framework for translating scientific research on sensory gardens into practical design guidelines for practitioners and decision makers. It synthesizes evidence on how horticultural elements and sensory stimulation can be structured to support human health and well-being.",
      "why": "It bridges the gap between academic findings and landscape design practice, providing a structured approach to turn theoretical health benefits of nature into actionable design decisions."
